  "step_2": "The individual states that Lottery B is clearly attractive because they will win 2400 Euros in every case. They argue that even though Lottery A might yield 100 Euros more in some cases, the risk of losing everything (0 Euros) is too high. The individual does not explicitly mention probabilities or compare the likelihood of favorable outcomes. Instead, the justification focuses on the certainty of winning 2400 Euros in B versus the risk in A. The deliberation centers on risk aversion and certainty, not on comparing the probabilities of favorable outcomes. Thus, the individual considers the certainty and potential loss in A, but does not reference or evaluate the probability of favorable outcomes as per the decision reason.",
